1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,447
Khmer folk tale, let's read entire story <color=orange><b>The Rice Seeds</b></color>.

2
00:00:10,447 --> 00:00:18,890
Long ago there was a king wanting to find successor.

3
00:00:20,027 --> 00:00:31,343
King ordered to give each citizen a basket of rice seeds to plant and set appointment:

4
00:00:31,343 --> 00:00:45,619
Whoever harvests most rice will inherit throne, whoever has no rice seeds to submit will be punished.

5
00:00:48,935 --> 00:01:00,512
Little Chom received rice seeds, took good care but seeds did not sprout.

6
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:11,088
At harvest, everyone noisily carried rice to capital to submit to king.

7
00:01:11,188 --> 00:01:16,097
Chom worried went before king, knelt down:

8
00:01:16,097 --> 00:01:22,208
- Your Majesty! I cannot make seeds sprout.

9
00:01:22,121 --> 00:01:27,201
Everyone was stunned by Chom's confession.

10
00:01:27,201 --> 00:01:31,808
But king helped little boy up.

11
00:01:31,808 --> 00:01:36,729
He asked if anyone else had dead rice seeds.

12
00:01:35,729 --> 00:01:38,890
No one answered.

13
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:42,667
Then king said:

14
00:01:42,552 --> 00:01:46,362
- Before giving rice seeds, I had boiled them well.

15
00:01:46,362 --> 00:01:49,415
How can those seeds grow?

16
00:01:49,415 --> 00:01:54,758
Those full carts of rice were not harvested from my rice seeds!

17
00:01:54,758 --> 00:01:57,686
Then king continued:

18
00:01:57,686 --> 00:02:01,936
- Honesty is the most noble quality of human.

19
00:02:01,936 --> 00:02:07,464
I will pass throne to this honest and brave little boy.

20
00:02:07,464 --> 00:02:13,071
Chom inherited throne and became a wise and good king.

